A||||3||Pretender||roller rockers, will i have to...?||||10||
Z||000000||Pretender||01-12-2000||04:46 AM||||I'm about to replace the intakes', so i thought as long as i have the ability to change them over will i have to adjust the valves or something?, i thought they were a "bolt-on" but a guy at work tonight told me that i would have to crank the engine over buy hand(ratchet on crank?) and torq till my hands bleed over and over again. Who's installed a set of these? i don't want the $300 kind, but whats the difference between them and the cheaper ones? thanks...<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Eric||01-12-2000||03:31 PM||||The difference between those and the expensive kind is big.  Full roller rockers provide less friction.  Roller tipped rockers don't do much at all.  There is no significant improvement over stock rockers.  At most there would be 1 or 2 horsepower gained at high rpm, very high rpm.  There are a ton of other things you could spend your money on before you should worry about roller tipped rockers.  I wouldn't know much about installing them in the car because I put new rockers in when I rebuilt the engine and, guess what, they weren't roller tipped!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||01-13-2000||03:00 AM||||If you're not using the full rollers then the other choice is for stamped steel or cast chromoly.  The cast ones are still a LOT cheaper than rollers and much better than stamped.  Better alloy and tighter dimensions.  Roller tip are mostly to make you feel good 'cause they have 'roller' in their name.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||01-13-2000||03:11 AM||||Oh yeah  how to put them on.  Stick them all in finger tight.  Turn the engine until #4 is in between in and out (both valves move, stop with them even).  Tighten the rocker nut while spinning the pushrod with the other hand.  When the pushrod stops turning twist the nut another 1/2 turn. Do the other rocker.  Turn the engine until the rockers on #5 center and set #2 rockers. Follow through entire firing order, taking care and time so not to bleed on engine.||||reg||1
